  "body": "Fixes from the final review:\n\n- An alert with no TestEventId now counts as a match, so a negative can't pass on output the judge couldn't read (unit tests).\n- Rejects control characters in fixtures; repaired the corrupted User field (CORP\\alice) in 14 Sysmon fixtures.\n- Rule gaps, each pinned by a positive fixture that failed first: every -EncodedCommand prefix (-Encoded), the LSASS filter now uses install paths (a renamed MsMpEng.exe fires), and auditd EXECVE also checks a3 (bash -l -c).\n- A case-variant positive for the Conditional Access rule (exact-match case-insensitivity on both engines).\n- Docs: what the Elasticsearch engine does and doesn't prove, case semantics per target, auditd decoding assumption.\n- portfolio.yaml status: complete (owner confirmed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
